notes={
379269:('parked_bounded_nonfinding','BCH code is binary primitive narrow-sense, roots alpha^1 through alpha^(2t-2), extended by parity. Formal-power-series root has constant coefficient1. Source Conjecture2 already verifies m<=6; our smaller diagnostic adds no new result. Need an all-m 2-adic divisibility mechanism, not more parameter certificates.'),
379291:('parked_scope_gap','Ostrik Conjecture3.2 uses modulating spaces and arbitrary nondegenerate pairings over every field. Etingof–Eu ordinary/modified preprojective-algebra result is a lead, not a verified full bridge for arbitrary modulation. No new Koszul/flatness proof or finite degree-rank computation completed.'),
379296:('parked_sustained_nonfinding','Exact primary scope q=3 mod4, adjacency nonzero-square quadrance (dx)^2+(dy)^2. All q-point cliques/cocliques through zero for q3,7,11,19 are lines. All33880 F3-linear3-subspaces of F27^2 checked;28 homogeneous ones are F27-lines. Nonlinear q27 and larger nonprime q remain unsearched. Need a nonlinear extremizer or a genuinely new direction theorem.'),
379528:('excluded_known_resolution','Ferber–Glebov–Krivelevich–Naor arXiv1210.7618 Theorems1.2–1.5 explicitly settle source Conjecture1.1. Theorem1.5 gives c/10<=threshold<=c+epsilon at p=c log(n)/n for c>1600; Theorem1.2 covers p=omega(log(n)/n). Relevant theorem statements and final proof adaptation read. No finite n mismatch can refute a Theta asymptotic statement.'),
379545:('parked_bounded_nonfinding','Primary Conjecture1.5; Definition3.2 at m=0 and M1–M4 fixed, including exact column restrictions. Exhaustive all arrays n2..6 gives matching restricted counts. Pfaffian/constant-term identities in the source are reformulations, not read as proofs of the equality. Need uniform identity evaluation; no new route beyond enumerations.'),
379584:('excluded_literal_defect_intended_open','Raw MathDB uses floor(lg n); source Conjecture7.2 uses ceiling(lg n). n=3 has no parity3-coloring and has parity4-colorings; this confirms the transcription defect, not a credited refutation. Intended ceiling conjecture remains parked; small exact parity-path check only, not strong parity-walk optimization.'),
379673:('parked_continuous_geometry','Primary Conger conjecture concerns every piecewise differentiable elliptic norm, not a finite graph invariant. Source norms l1+lambda*l2 attain2n in known ranges. No new dual supporting-functional configuration or all-n inequality found. No claim that bounded SMT searches clear the continuum quantifier.'),
379837:('parked_bounded_nonfinding','Complement connectivity implication has one uniform positive constantC. Atlas search finds no Reed violator at orders2..7, so the antecedent never activates there. It does not boundC or settle Reed; constructing one small graph is insufficient unless it gives a true asymptotic obstruction.'),
379845:('parked_source_search_gap','Exact N(S) quantifies all triangulation sizes above a threshold; it is not the flip diameter of one finite triangulation graph. Source Conjecture3 identifies six surfaces; no new full triangulation generator or all-size stabilization test was implemented. Finite-surface counterexample coverage is0; material implementation gap, not a novelty clearance.'),
379908:('excluded_known_resolution','Blokhuis–Mazzocca arXiv0911.4370 Proposition7 and Example2 give the exact odd-q minimum. Statement, incidence-formula setup and dual Proposition8 proof route read. Exhaustive translation-normalized line unions q3,5,7 reproduce minima7,17,31, with9,625,117649 configurations.'),
379969:('parked_public_resolution_lead','Literal source omits noncomplete condition; complete graphs give an elementary excluded-domain defect. Corrected Bollobas–Nikiforov assertion has a September2026 public Lean-resolution lead at ShengtongZhang-alt/BN. That proof body was NOT fetched/audited here, so no verified full-resolution assertion. Atlas noncomplete spectral check is floating point only.'),
380100:('excluded_routine_primary_bridge','Pfeifle0707.3010v2 Theorem4.11 gives the entire feasible root locus; equation7 and outer-oval angle description yield the literal imaginary bound by a one-variable derivative. Full ordinary bridge in outputs/snn-routine-bridge.md; no novelty or Lean credit. Kolbl2025 restricted theorem is not evidence against this stronger older subsumer.'),
380202:('parked_topological_scope','Primary Conjecture2 concerns minimal-page book embeddings realizing the global link minimum; neither arbitrary many-page book embeddings nor a planar drawing settles it. No complete spatial-isotopy/link minimization algorithm or full-scope bridge recovered; no bounded certificate claim.'),
380330:('parked_source_definition_gap','Prime, pure, bicoloured parity class and alternance are source-specific. The excerpted record alone cannot support testing arbitrary circle graphs. Primary PDF acquired, but no verified implementation of all four predicates completed. Exact finite counterexample search coverage0; cycle-double-cover consequences do not grant a proof.'),
380350:('parked_quantifier_prior_gap','Source wording largest system versus a largest system matters. Li–Meagher1201.4375 final discussion explicitly gives a non-almost-uniform maximum(10,4) system and proposes the weaker existence version. This does not refute the MathDB existence reading. Exact max-clique comparison for all partitions n3..7,k2..n-1 finds equal ordinary and almost-uniform optima. No general proof.'),
380376:('excluded_refuted_in_source','Source Conjecture1.1 is explicitly countered in Section3; the distinct nonequilateral-triangle question is Conjecture1.2 and outside this reservation. No credit for repeating the recorded plane coloring.'),
380444:('parked_bounded_nonfinding','Primary parameters l_i are bounding-box side lengths; total v=sum redundancies in a cell construction. All translation classes of planar polyominoes through9 cells were generated; every area maximizer has totalv0 and passes the recorded row-plus-perpendicular-arms test. General-d recursive decomposition not proved; source says only parts of the claim follow from Theorem4.'),
380616:('excluded_known_refutation','Noel2609.23291 Theorem1.1 and its explicit14-vertex graph/list construction refute the exact partial-list-coloring conjecture: chi_l=3, t2, maximum9<28/3. Actual theorem and proof conclusion read. No new result or formalization undertaken.'),
380674:('excluded_known_resolution','Zeilberger math/9811108v2, Proof of a conjecture of Chan, Robbins, and Yuen, proves the exact Catalan-product volume formula using Morris constant-term identity. Primary short paper acquired and theorem/formula read. No new credit for redoing this classical1998 result.'),
380808:('parked_bounded_nonfinding','Moore graphs here attain the girth Moore bound, not arbitrary cages. Exact matrix-tree determinants for atlas graphs2..7 and20000 seeded random(10,15)-graphs find no improvement over Petersen2000. Random comparisons are not exhaustive; no uniform spanning-tree extremal proof found.'),
381005:('parked_continuous_design_prior_gap','Unitary2-design means exact unweighted finite set, with all Haar second moments. The conjectural d^4-d^2 bound differs from the proved d^4-2d^2+2 lower bound. Later construction lead not body-verified; no false resolution asserted from conflating these bounds. Continuous unitary entries not exhaustively searched.'),
381027:('excluded_formulation_defect','Source defines a double-star as exactly six vertices, degrees3,3,1,1,1,1 and requires leaves independent in ambient graph. Exhaustive biconnected subcubic atlas test finds noncubic failures, including once-subdivided K4(5 vertices,7 edges): no double-star fits; an even-cycle part has at most4 edges and a matching at most2. This is an elementary noncubic formulation defect, excluded from credit. All tested cubic cases pass; snark route remains hard.'),
381104:('parked_analytic_source_gap','Weighted spherical operator and alternatives in the source proposition must be recovered before a numerical eigenvalue discretization means anything. Literal statement and source conjecture acquired; no rigorous Sturm–Liouville comparison or uniform-kappa spectral certificate completed.'),
381127:('parked_capped_decision_tree_search','Fixed alpha=1/a with integera; possible defective sets have cardinality AT LEASTk, queries answer by density, leaf outputs an element common to all remaining possibilities. Exact minimax rows saved throughn7; larger search ended exit137 under caps. Completed rows agree with Theorem6 bound. No claim that incomplete n8/n9 cases ran to completion; detailed algorithm-branch equality still needed for any improved bound.'),
381160:('excluded_source_corollary','The source explicitly derives Ilic–Stevanovic Volkmann spectral-moment conjecture from its greedy-tree and majorization theorems. Actual Conjecture1 and corollary discussion read. Exhaustive unlabeled trees2..13 at moments4,6,8 reproduce known cases; no new proof credit.'),
381163:('parked_source_geometry_gap','Radial line-of-sight conventions include angular coordinates up to3pi and repeated intersections. A permutation-of-semi-bar-lengths test would not model this semi-arc class. No verified generic-position representation checker completed; exact finite coverage0. Material semantic gap recorded rather than a surrogate search.'),
381176:('parked_complexity_problem','Input is the full linear-extension graph; its size, not underlying poset size, controls polynomial time. A finite set of posets cannot falsify the complexity assertion. Source Proposition7 gives quasi-polynomial time. Later Knauer–Nisse work is an adjacent closure-system result, not verified as solving this exact question.'),
381184:('parked_symbolic_definition_gap','The two polynomial counts and partitions arise from source Zn-curve/divisor operators. A count depending only on multiplicities cannot be assumed from the abbreviated record. No complete exact divisor/orbit enumerator or leading-coefficient formula recovered; finite search coverage0 and no new theorem.'),
381203:('excluded_refuted_in_source','Primary paper Section2 explicitly constructs counterexamples to the exact Akbari upper bound. Theorem3 computes gamma_R prime(K_r,s)=2r when r<s and2r-1 whenr=s; proof and disjoint-union comparison inspected. Already a known refutation; do not recredit a small graph.'),
381218:('parked_bounded_nonfinding_domain_caution','Source uses odd-prime zero-sum theory; p2 in a literal all-primes paraphrase is an endpoint defect, not a candidate. Exhaustive origin-normalized caps in F3^3 find maximum support9, hence maximum zero-sum-free sequence length18 when multiplicities<=2; this reproduces s_1=19. No all-odd-prime bound proved.'),
381254:('parked_resolution_announcement','Source following Conjecture1.8 explicitly says Stiebitz and Toft announced an affirmative resolution. Their full theorem/proof was not recovered in this pass; announcement is not a completed body comparison. Complexity claim has no single bounded-instance counterexample. Do not invest without finishing that prior-art check.'),
381393:('excluded_refuted_in_source','Review source Conjecture2.9 and subsequent discussion report failure via three compact convex sets in R3. The raw statement itself already says false. No new projection-limit counterexample or credited formalization.'),
381397:('parked_structured_nonfinding','Exact subspace distance is2k-2, so intersections have dimension<=1. Forq2,k4, all200787 RREF4-subspaces of F2^8 were tested as one-subspace extensions of the257-word lifted Gabidulin-plus-vertical code; no extension. All32896 seed pairs verified. This is an extension search for one known code, not an optimum proof or all-code search.'),
381430:('parked_bounded_nonfinding','Source normalizes h by volume and uses normalized Laplacian spectral gap. Atlas distance-regular graphs through7 vertices satisfy the diagnostic inequalities. Eigenvalues were floating point; no exact counterexample. Source-mentioned generalized-hexagon cases require much larger exact cut optimization, not completed.'),
381469:('parked_sustained_nonfinding','Gamma_e is the minimum cardinality of a maximal matching, not maximum matching. Exact atlas tests and separate degree-sequence enumeration of regular graphs are retained. No violation found. Need a structural deficit proof uniformly inDelta or a nontrivial exact equality obstruction; no such lemma obtained. Completed coverage in logs only.'),
381502:('excluded_known_resolution','Keusch2303.02611 Theorem1 proves the exact1–2–3 statement for graphs without isolated edges; connected order>=3 is a direct subclass. Actual theorem and proof case setup read, not merely the title. No credited repetition.'),
381552:('excluded_known_witness_bridge','Exact formal counterexample is graph Db[ on5 vertices and6 edges, degree sequence1,2,3,3,3. Independent Lean proof establishes literal eventual locality after every number of isolates, edge count, minimum degree and nonisomorphism to sourceH5. HOWEVER authors older pinned public catalogue already labels this exact graph LA GA, giving an immediate prior-art bridge. Excluded as known-witness routine consequence. Packet is research evidence, not a new-credit candidate.'),
381596:('parked_infinite_lattice_condition','Delta_m is an infimum over every nonzero lattice vector. A finite lattice-vector sample cannot verify the nonvanishing hypothesis. No construction with a proved positive infimum or a general impossibility proof obtained; no new certificate.'),
381703:('parked_sustained_nonfinding','Source allows loopless multigraphs; simple-atlas search alone would miss scope. Added exhaustive labeled multigraphs on3/4 vertices with every multiplicity0..3, all admissiblep,q and all sub-multiplicity partitions:64/4096 graphs,27/864 classII, no obstruction. Need a global balancing argument retaining degree saturation in both classI parts.'),
381704:('parked_sustained_nonfinding','Quantifier is EACH maximum matching in a regular classII graph. Exact atlas test plus all maximum matchings in Petersen and two once-subdividedK4 blocks joined by a bridge find completion. In bridged cubic example all4 perfect matchings pass; resistance2 with49 optimal deletions. Need larger nonperfect-maximum-matching regular graphs or a new edge-color exchange theorem.')}
